   "id": "T1",
   "judgement": {
    "kind": "answered",
    "quotes": [
     "Nothing when the name fails condition 1 of A3 rule 5. Otherwise a `SourceRead`: one `SourceFile`, and the bytes that were judged when it is ready. A ready `SourceFile` carries in `modified` the modification time A1 takes from the opened file, so its caller reads no metadata of its own.",
     "A file that is read takes its modification time from one metadata reading of the file that was\nopened, the one whose bytes are read, taken after the opening and before the read; A7 rule 4 gives its\nform, and a delivery uses that time under A2 rule 3.",
     "A file's modification time is converted to the same form before it is compared or delivered, dropping\n   any fraction finer than a microsecond toward the earlier instant."
    ],
    "later_state": null,
    "divergence": "",
    "why": "The texts require the caller to use the ready SourceFile's `modified` value captured from the same opened file as the bytes and define it as UTC without an offset at microsecond precision, truncating finer fractions toward the earlier instant.",
